WEBVTT

1
00:00:04.150 --> 00:00:09.163
Big report out this week. Alan Milburn.

2
00:00:09.163 --> 00:00:11.478
Nearly a million young people not earning or learning,

3
00:00:11.478 --> 00:00:14.024
and he's got a ten-year plan to fix it.

4
00:00:14.674 --> 00:00:17.010
This is my niece Jamie's door.

5
00:00:17.010 --> 00:00:18.874
19. Bright girl.

6
00:00:18.874 --> 00:00:21.620
Hasn't been past the front gate since March.

7
00:00:22.270 --> 00:00:23.884
And she's not idle.

8
00:00:23.884 --> 00:00:27.092
Nearly half of young people out of work and learning

9
00:00:27.092 --> 00:00:30.481
have a diagnosed mental health or neurodevelopmental disorder.

10
00:00:30.481 --> 00:00:33.608
Anxiety is one of the most common.

11
00:00:34.258 --> 00:00:35.851
Milburn's plan?

12
00:00:35.851 --> 00:00:41.060
A named adviser in 14 days. A plan in four weeks.

13
00:00:41.060 --> 00:00:42.884
Somewhere to go.

14
00:00:42.884 --> 00:00:45.428
Jamie can't even get to the end of her drive.

15
00:00:46.078 --> 00:00:48.192
If she keeps saying no,

16
00:00:48.192 --> 00:00:52.502
the report says she would ultimately lose any support money.

17
00:00:52.502 --> 00:00:54.586
The girl who can't open the door...

18
00:00:54.586 --> 00:00:57.632
is going to get docked for not being able to walk through it.

19
00:00:58.282 --> 00:01:03.751
The new service reaches every part of England by 2029.

20
00:01:03.751 --> 00:01:05.684
Jamie will be 22.

21
00:01:06.334 --> 00:01:07.607
So what's missing?

22
00:01:07.607 --> 00:01:08.716
The bridge.

23
00:01:08.716 --> 00:01:11.796
Jamie needs someone who will come to her first.

24
00:01:11.796 --> 00:01:13.439
A message, then a call,

25
00:01:13.439 --> 00:01:15.824
and then a meeting at her place.

26
00:01:16.474 --> 00:01:18.527
And people are already doing this.

27
00:01:18.527 --> 00:01:21.993
In Hertfordshire, Forever Young People

28
00:01:21.993 --> 00:01:25.279
mentor young people one to one,

29
00:01:25.279 --> 00:01:29.786
and set out to meet each of them where they are,

30
00:01:29.786 --> 00:01:31.209
physically, emotionally.

31
00:01:31.209 --> 00:01:33.452
Now that's what I call a bridge.

32
00:01:34.102 --> 00:01:37.587
Fund these foundations and charities

33
00:01:37.587 --> 00:01:39.390
who are already doing it,

34
00:01:39.390 --> 00:01:42.996
and that bridge will get built now.

35
00:01:42.996 --> 00:01:44.899
And when she's ready to cross it,

36
00:01:44.899 --> 00:01:47.192
there needs to be a job there for her.

37
00:01:47.842 --> 00:01:49.475
That's where I come in.

38
00:01:49.475 --> 00:01:52.639
I've got a five-person joinery, a bench, a kettle

39
00:01:52.639 --> 00:01:54.162
and a job going.

40
00:01:54.162 --> 00:01:56.125
What I haven't got is...

41
00:01:56.125 --> 00:01:59.080
a year's wages for someone who might need three months

42
00:01:59.080 --> 00:02:00.932
just to get through the door.

43
00:02:01.582 --> 00:02:02.093
Meanwhile,

44
00:02:02.093 --> 00:02:08.054
Milburn's own report says that around £460 million of levy money

45
00:02:08.054 --> 00:02:12.112
is being kept back by the Treasury this year.

46
00:02:12.112 --> 00:02:16.760
And his new money won't start working until 2027.

47
00:02:17.410 --> 00:02:22.203
Let's pay the first year's wages for our young people,

48
00:02:22.203 --> 00:02:27.919
and give that money to small businesses and SMEs like mine,

49
00:02:27.919 --> 00:02:30.246
with a real job at the end of it.

50
00:02:30.246 --> 00:02:31.940
Start now.

51
00:02:32.590 --> 00:02:35.618
Someone has to knock on the door first.

52
00:02:35.618 --> 00:02:36.776
Com'mon!
